Welcome to the **Open-Source Satellite Platform**🛰️, an open-source community initiated by **BUPT**.

Our goal is to share satellite-related software, resources, and knowledge, and to provide a platform for collaboration, discussion, and innovation in satellite computing and applications.

## 💬 Discussions

We have enabled **GitHub Discussions** as a place for communication and knowledge sharing.

👉 **Discussions:** [https://github.com/orgs/Satellite-OSS-BUPT/discussions]

We will regularly post:

- 📢 Project updates and announcements
- 📚 Satellite-related knowledge and technical content
- 🔧 Interesting open-source tools and projects
- 🛰️ Resources related to satellite computing and applications

Everyone is welcome to join the discussion!

If you have ideas, suggestions, or specific needs, feel free to create a new discussion. You are also welcome to introduce and promote your own **satellite-related tools, software, datasets, or open-source projects** to the community.

## 📦 Our Repositories

We maintain multiple repositories covering different aspects of satellite computing and applications. They will be continuously updated as new resources and projects become available.

### 📚 Satellite Resources

A collection of useful resources related to satellites and satellite computing, including:

- Papers from major conferences and journals
- Open-source satellite tools and frameworks
- Useful datasets, projects, and technical resources

### 📊 Software Evaluation Platform

Tools and platforms for evaluating software and computational workloads.

These repositories are intended to support experiments, performance evaluation, and research on computational tasks in satellite environments.

### 💻 Application Software

Open-source application software and example code designed for or capable of running on satellites.

We hope these projects can provide useful references and building blocks for developing and deploying future satellite applications.

## 🤝 Contributing

Contributions and suggestions are always welcome.

You can participate by:

- Opening a **Discussion** to share an idea or request
- Recommending useful papers, tools, datasets, or projects
- Introducing your own satellite-related open-source work
- Reporting issues or proposing improvements
- Contributing code to our repositories

We hope to build an open and collaborative ecosystem for **satellite software, computing, and applications**.

---

**Explore. Share. Build for Space. 🛰️**
